Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (v1.4.2) using npm
- Updated package.json with the new dependency
- Updated package-lock.json to lock the dependency versions

### Code Changes
Modified: `src/app/layout.tsx`
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';`
- Added the `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the children
- Preserved all existing code structure, styling, and formatting

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart):
1. Installed the @vercel/analytics package using npm
2. Added the Analytics component to the root layout file (src/app/layout.tsx)
3. Placed the component at the end of the body tag for optimal performance
4. Used the framework-specific import from '@vercel/analytics/next' for Next.js integration

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully without errors
✅ Linting passed for the modified layout.tsx file (no new errors introduced)
✅ TypeScript compilation completed without issues
